&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Food Safety &amp;amp; Quality Assurance team and play a key role in maintaining the highest standards across our operations. In this dynamic position, you&#39;ll take ownership of day-to-day compliance activities, ensuring processes are completed accurately and consistently. You&#39;ll lead UK FSQA reporting, providing valuable insights that support business performance and regulatory compliance. Working closely with the wider FSQA team, you&#39;ll also contribute to exciting food safety and quality improvement projects, helping to drive continuous improvement and uphold our commitment to excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Be Doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reporting and Data Analysis: Generate comprehensive UK FSQA reports, including monthly summaries, a weekly FSQA newsletter (GMP, Ice, Destructive Testing, System Compliance), and routine KPI updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document Control Management: Own and maintain the UK Document Control process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Audit Compliance &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement: Monitor site audit compliance, including tracking GMP scores and updating frequency risk assessments, while leading site initiatives to achieve and sustain high performance scores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Complaint Oversight: Manage the full lifecycle of UK and IE customer complaints, including detailed investigation, root cause analysis, and proactive trending.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certification Readiness: Support the BRCGS GAP Analysis and maintain robust systems and documentation to ensure continuous site audit readiness, for UK and IE&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality Assurance Project Leadership: Drive independent projects and perform ad hoc tasks focused on maintaining and enhancing compliance with food safety and quality standards. Oversee routine processes such as temperature monitoring and calibration checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training Support: Support the development and delivery of site training programs necessary to uphold quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Risk Communication: Ensure clear, timely, and effective communication and escalation of all quality and safety risks and issues to relevant stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in a quality/ compliance role within food &amp;amp; beverage or similar industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of experience in a people management role, demonstrating the ability to lead, motivate, and develop teams effectively!&lt;br&gt;Proficiency in using quality management software or tools for data analysis and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience HACCP Level 3 &amp;amp; Food Safety Level 3 Degree in food science, food technology or a related field preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in using G-Suite Software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in managing direct reports and line management responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident and effective communicator with strong interpersonal, relationship building and negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will get in return:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;● 70% off HelloFresh or Green Chef boxes&lt;br&gt;● Company pension scheme&lt;br&gt;● Gym membership&lt;br&gt;● Bupa private medical insurance (including dental &amp;amp; family cover options)&lt;br&gt;● Mental health first aiders and an employee assistance programme&lt;br&gt;● Dog friendly office! (London site only)&lt;br&gt;● Nursery support scheme&lt;br&gt;● Cycle to work scheme&lt;br&gt;● Group Life Assurance&lt;/p&gt;
