&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you up for the challenge?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please submit your complete application below including your salary expectations and earliest starting date.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;After submitting an application our team will review this and get back to you within 5 business days.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Factor Europe is scaling rapidly, and as the complexity of our product offering grows, we are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Sr. Manager, Menu Performance&lt;/strong&gt; to optimize the performance of our weekly menu plan and surrounding processes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a data-driven, hands-on building role. You will decide what tools, systems, and processes we need to optimize our weekly processes, and use all of the AI tools at your disposal to develop / optimize them. You’ll be the ultimate owner of our weekly product cycle: which means optimizing our menu for maximal engagement and retention of our customers, as well as simplifying / automating as much of our internal process as possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether you’re analytical supply chain master who wants more exposure to product/customer, a systems thinker who loves building and improving processes, or a technical generalist who wants to push the boundaries of what’s newly possible with AI - this is a chance to supercharge one of Europe’s fastest-growing food-tech brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize menu performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve our menu planning model: Refine the models that architect our weekly menu—optimizing for customer engagement and retention within&amp;nbsp;real constraints: seasonality, cost targets, and production capacity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find out what actually drives outcomes: Run correlation and driver analysis on which menu attributes genuinely move engagement and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Model the commercial impact: Understand and forecast how menu decisions land on cost per meal and profitability to course-correct early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the weekly menu cycle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate customer data into action: Own the weekly menu review, turning customer ratings and qualitative feedback into insights the Culinary and Kitchen Operations teams can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the process reliably: Ensure menus are built and uploaded on time, coordinating across R&amp;amp;D, Supply Chain, and Production as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own recipe/menu data quality: Challenge our data hygiene practices and implement the processes and controls that ensure our data is complete and accurate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-style: italic;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the tools and automate the work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automate meal onboarding: Take our concept-to-launch process apart, find the unnecessary manual steps, and eliminate or automate them to&amp;nbsp;improve speed to market. Expect to build software and write scripts to get there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and extend the Product tool stack: Take our existing tools and improve them, consolidate them, and build what’s missing. Build systems that survive without you in the room.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder: You are comfortable with ambiguity. You don’t need a playbook to be effective; you are excited to write it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-obsessed: You’re fluent enough to query and QA data yourself, and can create data visualizations that separate signal from noise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker: You don’t just fix a problem; you fix the process that allowed the problem to happen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured and process-oriented: You can quickly spot the bottlenecks in a process and picture the improvements concretely enough to build toward them; you love creating issue trees and driving to the root cause of problems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native: You’re on the cutting edge of what tools are available and have built things beyond what your formal background should allow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency: You don’t get stuck easily: you ask why, you find workarounds, and you hustle to keep the project on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
